\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.1}{\ignorespaces The unit sphere $S$. The constraint $|\vek  {u}|=1$ confines the admissible increments $\mathrm  {d}\vek  {u}$ to the tangent plane at $\vek  {u}$, so stationarity of $f(\vek  {u})=\vek  {u}\cdot \vek  {A}\vek  {u}$ requires $\vek  {A}\vek  {u}$ to be orthogonal to that whole plane, hence parallel to $\vek  {u}$ itself. This is \eqr  {3.22}: an extremum of the quadratic form is a principal direction.}}{116}{figure.557}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:31}{{3.1}{116}{The unit sphere $S$. The constraint $|\bu |=1$ confines the admissible increments $\dl \bu $ to the tangent plane at $\bu $, so stationarity of $f(\bu )=\ip {\bu }{\bA \bu }$ requires $\bA \bu $ to be orthogonal to that whole plane, hence parallel to $\bu $ itself. This is \eqr {3.22}: an extremum of the quadratic form is a principal direction}{figure.557}{}}
