\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {B}{\ignorespaces Material versus principal directions in simple shear. The solid arrow is the material fibre $\cc@accent {"705E}{\vek  {E}}_{1}$: it is decided in $\kappa $ and its image is $\vek  {e}_{1}$, unstretched and unturned for every $\gamma $. The grey arrow is the material fibre $\cc@accent {"705E}{\vek  {E}}_{2}$, whose image tilts and lengthens by $\sqrt  {1+\gamma ^{2}}$. The dashed arrow is the principal direction $\vek  {u}_{1}$: it is \emph  {not} attached to any fixed matter, and as $\gamma $ grows it sweeps across the fibres at the rate computed in Remark~\ref {rem:notmaterial}.}}{131}{figure.619}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:matvec}{{B}{131}{Material versus principal directions in simple shear. The solid arrow is the material fibre $\hbE _{1}$: it is decided in $\kappa $ and its image is $\be _{1}$, unstretched and unturned for every $\gamma $. The grey arrow is the material fibre $\hbE _{2}$, whose image tilts and lengthens by $\sqrt {1+\gamma ^{2}}$. The dashed arrow is the principal direction $\bu _{1}$: it is \emph {not} attached to any fixed matter, and as $\gamma $ grows it sweeps across the fibres at the rate computed in Remark~\ref {rem:notmaterial}}{figure.619}{}}
