\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {A}{\ignorespaces Left: the reference space does not move, so the vertical arrow on that side is the identity, while the configuration at $t$ is carried to the one at $t+\mathrm  {d}t$ by $\vek  {x}\DOTSB \mapstochar \rightarrow \vek  {x}+\mathrm  {d}t\,\vek  {v}$, whose gradient is $\vek  {I}+\mathrm  {d}t\,\vek  {L}$. Commutativity of the square is $\vek  {F}(t+\mathrm  {d}t)=(\vek  {I}+\mathrm  {d}t\,\vek  {L})\vek  {F}(t)$, which is \eqr  {4.3}. Right: changing the reference from $\kappa $ to $\kappa '$ replaces $\vek  {F}$ by $\vek  {F}\vek  {K}$ with $\vek  {K}$ fixed in time. The triangle commutes, and since $\cc@accent {"705F}\vek  {K}=\cc@accent {"705E}{\vek  {O}}$ the factor cancels in $\cc@accent {"705F}\vek  {F}\vek  {F}^{-1}$: the two references disagree about $\vek  {F}$ and about $\cc@accent {"705F}\vek  {F}$, but not about $\vek  {L}$.}}{203}{figure.852}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ch4comm}{{A}{203}{Left: the reference space does not move, so the vertical arrow on that side is the identity, while the configuration at $t$ is carried to the one at $t+\dl t$ by $\bx \mapsto \bx +\dl t\,\bv $, whose gradient is $\I +\dl t\,\bL $. Commutativity of the square is $\bF (t+\dl t)=(\I +\dl t\,\bL )\bF (t)$, which is \eqr {4.3}. Right: changing the reference from $\kappa $ to $\kappa '$ replaces $\bF $ by $\bF \bK $ with $\bK $ fixed in time. The triangle commutes, and since $\dot \bK =\hOb $ the factor cancels in $\dot \bF \bF ^{-1}$: the two references disagree about $\bF $ and about $\dot \bF $, but not about $\bL $}{figure.852}{}}
