\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {C}{\ignorespaces The entire meaning of $\vek  {D}$, read off two material fibres that are momentarily perpendicular at $\vek  {x}$. Their lengths change at the logarithmic rates $\vek  {m}_{i}\cdot \vek  {D}\vek  {m}_{i}$, which are the diagonal components of $\vek  {D}$ in the basis $\{\vek  {m}_{1},\vek  {m}_{2}\}$, by \eqr  {4.15}. The right angle between them closes at the rate $2\,\vek  {m}_{1}\cdot \vek  {D}\vek  {m}_{2}$, twice the off-diagonal component, by \eqr  {4.21}. Drawn with $\vek  {W}=\vek  {O}$, so that the closing is shared equally; in general $\vek  {W}$ turns the pair bodily as well, and \eqr  {4.21} fixes only the sum.}}{217}{figure.904}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:Dmeaning}{{C}{217}{The entire meaning of $\bD $, read off two material fibres that are momentarily perpendicular at $\bx $. Their lengths change at the logarithmic rates $\bm _{i}\cdot \bD \bm _{i}$, which are the diagonal components of $\bD $ in the basis $\{\bm _{1},\bm _{2}\}$, by \eqr {4.15}. The right angle between them closes at the rate $2\,\bm _{1}\cdot \bD \bm _{2}$, twice the off-diagonal component, by \eqr {4.21}. Drawn with $\bW =\Ob $, so that the closing is shared equally; in general $\bW $ turns the pair bodily as well, and \eqr {4.21} fixes only the sum}{figure.904}{}}
