\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.2}{\ignorespaces A material region $P_{t}\subset \kappa _{t}$ traversed by a propagating surface $s$. The normal $\vek  {n}$ on $s$ points from $V^{-}$ into $V^{+}$ and $s$ advances at speed $u$ along it. Material crosses $s$ whenever $u\neq  \vek  {v}\cdot \vek  {n}$: the surface is then not made of the same particles from one instant to the next, and $V^{\pm }$ are non-material regions even though their union $P_{t}$ is material. This is why \eqr  {5.27}, and not \eqr  {5.15}, is the formula to apply to each half.}}{255}{figure.1034}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ch5shock}{{5.2}{255}{A material region $P_{t}\subset \kappa _{t}$ traversed by a propagating surface $s$. The normal $\bn $ on $s$ points from $V^{-}$ into $V^{+}$ and $s$ advances at speed $u$ along it. Material crosses $s$ whenever $u\neq \ip \bv \bn $: the surface is then not made of the same particles from one instant to the next, and $V^{\pm }$ are non-material regions even though their union $P_{t}$ is material. This is why \eqr {5.27}, and not \eqr {5.15}, is the formula to apply to each half}{figure.1034}{}}
